1
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,000
I've already watched

2
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:24,720
all your performances just now.

3
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:27,000
Generally speaking, there's no problem at all.

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,440
The only thing to note is

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,240
that your performances are still

6
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:35,690
not precise enough.

7
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,160
What do I always tell you?

8
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:40,760
A good performer

9
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:43,220
should be like an experienced boxer.

10
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:46,560
What do rookie boxers usually do?

11
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:54,400
They usually

12
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:56,490
throw wild punches,

13
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:57,880
but they might

14
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:59,520
not hit their opponents.

15
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:01,840
And an old...

16
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:15,480
Sorry.

17
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:17,320
I was just saying...

18
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:18,580
An experienced boxer.

19
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:20,240
Thank you.

20
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:22,600
And an experienced boxer

21
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:25,240
usually wins with a single strike.

22
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:28,560
So what you need to focus on now is

23
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:30,000
to be like an experienced boxer.

24
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,600
Precise.

25
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:33,620
You have to make sure what you want to perform

26
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:36,160
can be instantly felt by the audience.

27
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:38,580
Dismissed.

28
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:41,920
What's wrong with the director today?

29
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:43,320
Never seen her like this.

30
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:44,930
I don't know either.

31
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,780
Maybe she's not feeling well.

32
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:02,600
Good acting.

33
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:04,500
Let's take a break.

34
00:02:08,479 --> 00:02:09,160
Going to the restroom?

35
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:09,720
Let's go.

36
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:13,120
It still hurts.

37
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,640
My leg hurts so much.

38
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:20,280
What's wrong?

39
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:25,079
Nothing.

40
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:27,450
I accidentally cut myself last night.

41
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:29,640
Tell me the truth.

42
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:31,370
Did you fight with Meng Tejiao?

43
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:33,380
Don't mention him.

44
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:34,800
We are now

45
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:36,480
100% just colleagues.

46
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:39,400
Listen to me.

47
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:42,160
Hurting others or yourself is not okay.

48
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:44,560
What exactly happened between you two?

49
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:47,200
The hand injury is a minor thing.

50
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:48,480
You know,

51
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:51,000
the most ridiculous thing is the reason we fought.

52
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:51,930
He actually said

53
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:55,440
I always ask him rhetorical questions,

54
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,480
and his dignity was insulted.

55
00:02:57,920 --> 00:02:58,600
And then?

56
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:01,640
Then I asked him back,

57
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:04,600
"Why is your dignity so easily insulted?"

58
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:09,240
Brother,

59
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,080
be gentle.

60
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,040
Director.

61
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,800
Sandwiches from the new internet-famous shop nearby.

62
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:21,800
Jinxi's treat.

63
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:23,760
Oh my God, Jinxi, you're the best.

64
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:27,100
I was just getting hungry.

65
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:27,880
Thanks.

66
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:40,280
Thank you, Jinxi.

67
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:43,200
Let's go.

68
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:45,400
Director,

69
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,460
do you want a sandwich?

70
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:51,960
No, thank you.

71
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:57,640
She's starting to lose interest in you.

72
00:03:58,440 --> 00:03:59,300
Lose interest?

73
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:02,680
Jinxi,

74
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:04,560
as someone who's been there,

75
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:05,840
I must remind you.

76
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:07,920
The director's attention

77
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:09,980
won't stay on the same actor forever.

78
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:11,890
Just like how I used to be

79
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,800
the only leading man in her eyes.

80
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:16,160
Just like you are now.

81
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:18,160
But you're not the first,

82
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:19,720
and you won't be the last.

83
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:21,040
Jianshe,

84
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,220
our situations

85
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:24,000
might be a little different.

86
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:29,360
Trust me,

87
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,000
it's all the same.

88
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:35,240
Internet-famous shops will become outdated one day,

89
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,120
just like us.

90
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:38,920
Jinxi,

91
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,560
you'll get used to it.

92
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,460
Zhang Wanru and I broke up.

93
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:55,440
I know.

94
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:57,890
Because of the rhetorical questions.

95
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,730
Don't think this is a small matter.

96
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:05,040
Her tone of voice reveals her subtext.

97
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:06,800
The subtext of a rhetorical question

98
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:08,640
is treating the other person like a fool,

99
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,840
a ridiculous person.

100
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,920
I don't think it's that serious.

101
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:15,370
You can't even see the darkest parts of human nature.

102
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:17,080
How can you be a director?

103
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,080
You see.

104
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:23,620
Rhetorical questions are quite hurtful, aren't they?

105
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:25,450
Don't worry.

106
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,520
I won't let my personal life affect my work.

107
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:30,560
Outside the theater troupe, we'll treat each other like air.

108
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:32,090
It won't affect the troupe.

109
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:37,280
Obviously, you two are still mad at each other.

110
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:37,880
I'm not.

111
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,060
Even if you aren't,

112
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:44,000
I do know that Cousin

113
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:46,200
has a long cut on her hand.

114
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,120
I'm quite worried.

115
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:48,720
What cut?

116
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:50,530
You didn't know?

117
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:51,520
I didn't know.

118
00:05:51,920 --> 00:05:52,960
After we fought the day before yesterday,

119
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:53,890
I went to a hotel.

120
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,400
Could it be because...

121
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:58,810
Impossible.

122
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:02,180
She's not the type of girl who doesn't respect herself.

123
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,960
She wouldn't actually do something stupid, would she?

124
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:09,000
And you said you'd treat her like air.

125
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Aren't you quite worried about her?

126
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:13,040
I didn't.

127
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,040
I'm leaving now.

128
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:16,960
Hello, dear friends.

129
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:19,000
Welcome to Xiaobai's live stream.

130
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,200
Remember to like.

131
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:22,480
Don't forget to hit the like button.

132
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,960
Jin Xi is handsome every day.

133
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:29,080
I've never seen him in a bad state.

134
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:30,600
Hello, Feixin.

135
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:32,080
I am a musical fan

136
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,159
and also your fan.

137
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:34,640
I watched your live stream a couple of days ago.

138
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:36,600
You said you wouldn't date an actor

139
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:37,880
because you think it's unprofessional.

140
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,200
I totally agree with that.

141
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:40,680
I have a colleague.

142
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:43,840
Actually, we had contact before we became colleagues.

143
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:44,720
I don't deny

144
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,440
that I have feelings for him.

145
00:06:46,760 --> 00:06:48,760
And I feel he's interested in me too.

146
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:51,360
But I think it's unprofessional

147
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:53,240
and goes against my principles.

148
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:55,980
So I've been distancing myself from him lately.

149
00:06:56,159 --> 00:06:57,080
However,

150
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:59,440
I just can't let him go,

151
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:01,040
and I'm very torn.

152
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,600
Let's discuss it, friends.

153
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:06,560
What do you think should be done about this?

154
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:11,920
Is it a crime to date a colleague, I ask?

155
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:13,800
Why are you torn?

156
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:14,600
Just go for it.

157
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:19,060
They probably hid the fact that they're married with kids.

158
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,000
Zai Shui Yifang,

159
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,320
since you've asked this question,

160
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:25,840
it shows you are struggling with it.

161
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:27,640
It means your liking

162
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:28,600
and love for this person

163
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:30,800
have started to shake your principles.

164
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:31,760
What principles

165
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:32,680
or bottom lines?

166
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,000
In the face of true love,

167
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,730
they are not worth mentioning.

168
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:40,040
For example, just like Nie Xiaoqian and Ning Caichen.

169
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:42,850
Do you think Nie Xiaoqian would think so much?

170
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:43,840
Everyone should know

171
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:45,970
the musical I'm rehearsing right now.

172
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,200
If you keep pestering me, I'll call the property management.

173
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:52,730
Ning Jin,

174
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:54,770
I'll just say one thing.

175
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,720
Are you still mad at me?

176
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:58,760
Let the past go.

177
00:07:58,760 --> 00:07:59,440
I'm not mad.

178
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:00,120
No,

179
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:01,800
then why have you been hiding from me?

180
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:02,960
Even Jianshe can see

181
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:05,220
you've been giving me the cold shoulder.

182
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,840
Even though he doesn't know why.

183
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,440
I hope you can look

184
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:10,240
at our relationship professionally

185
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:12,000
and don't imagine romantic entanglements that don't exist.

186
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:12,560
No,

187
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:14,720
I think this feeling definitely exists.

188
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:15,840
You said one sentence.

189
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:17,370
You've exceeded the limit.

190
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:19,250
I'll say one last thing.

191
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:22,970
Ning Jin.

192
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:24,760
I love...

193
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:28,100
Ning Jin...

194
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,400
Ning Jin!

195
00:08:37,159 --> 00:08:37,640
Bro.

196
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:41,320
Is the Weibo banner copy for tomorrow

197
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:41,799
okay?

198
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:42,799
Hmm?

199
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,240
Anything is fine with me.

200
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,170
You guys decide.

201
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:49,000
Why do you look so out of it?

202
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:51,680
Do you remember

203
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,280
a friend

204
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,640
I told you about last time?

205
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:57,980
That friend of mine

206
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:59,280
followed your advice

207
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:01,330
and boldly confessed his love.

208
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,060
But he messed it up.

209
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:09,240
You mean the inspiration for your lyrics

210
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:11,260
failed in his confession?

211
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:12,120
'I love you'.

212
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,560
Of those three words,

213
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:15,080
he only said two.

214
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:17,640
And the other person shut him out.

215
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:23,600
That attitude says it all.

216
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:26,090
This friend of yours...

217
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:26,840
Attitude.

218
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:28,680
Right.

219
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:31,560
Was his confession too direct,

220
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:35,260
making the other person feel he wasn't serious enough?

221
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:36,960
Maybe.

222
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:44,620
Bro, what's wrong?

223
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:45,920
You've been doing this a lot lately,

224
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,240
running off in the middle of a sentence.

225
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:47,800
Bro!

226
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:00,360
Where are the others?

227
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:02,300
I sent everyone else away.

228
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,640
What are you up to now?

229
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,500
Please take a seat.

230
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:55,370
Ning Jin.

231
00:12:56,320 --> 00:12:56,960
I like you.

232
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:59,060
To express my love for you,

233
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:01,490
I merged our two musical styles together.

234
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,930
A perfect match, right?

235
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:10,960
No.

236
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:12,560
Ning Jin.

237
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:15,440
Ning Jin.

238
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:18,320
Ning Jin.

239
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:26,200
I'll just tell you right here.

240
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:27,330
You crossed my line.

241
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:30,640
Haven't I been crossing your line all along?

242
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:32,370
Then let me make it clear to you.

243
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:35,260
I will absolutely not date an actor from the troupe.

244
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:36,360
Why?

245
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:38,840
Because it's very unprofessional.

246
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:40,000
What about Jiao Ye and Big Cousin?

247
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,400
Aren't they a couple too?

248
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:42,960
It hasn't affected them.

249
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:44,380
That's different.

250
00:13:44,640 --> 00:13:47,320
They were already together before they joined the troupe.

251
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:48,640
They are together every day.

252
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:50,320
And their acting is better than anyone else's.

253
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:51,360
Why can't we?

254
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:53,770
Ning Jin.

255
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:55,440
Let me ask you.

256
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:58,690
Do you have feelings for me?

257
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,440
When we first met,

258
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:01,920
it was my fault.

259
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:04,200
And I've already apologized to you.

260
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:07,060
I never expected we'd run into each other again.

261
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,730
Do you have feelings for me?

262
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:14,090
We're from completely different worlds.

263
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:15,200
If Boss Wu

264
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,720
hadn't bypassed my permission

265
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:17,480
to sign you,

266
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:18,680
we wouldn't be working together now.

267
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:19,280
Ning Jin.

268
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,120
Besides,

269
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,250
I'm just asking you,

270
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:22,920
do you have feelings

271
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:24,080
for me or not?

272
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:24,800
I do.

273
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:29,580
I knew you had feelings for me.

274
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:35,980
Even if I do have feelings for you,

275
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:38,450
it's impossible for us to be together.

276
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:41,970
Because right now, you are still my actor.

277
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:55,080
Trudging day and night on Black Mountain,

278
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:56,840
in the soul-burying stream of locust trees.

279
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:59,000
A lonely soul suffers for a century.

280
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:00,960
Who can break this curse of life and death?

281
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:02,690
Did you guys see cousin Jiaoye?

282
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:04,360
No.

283
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:07,240
What's wrong?

284
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:14,760
You're really not getting back together?

285
00:15:14,760 --> 00:15:15,000
No.

286
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:15,960
Director.

287
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:18,400
I'm breaking up with him for good this time.

288
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:19,400
Stay by my side.

289
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:21,080
Okay.

290
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,640
Zhang Wanru, stop right there!

291
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:25,320
Meng Tejiao, are you done?

292
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:43,440
Do you remember this?

293
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:48,290
I bought this for you the first time we went to Disney.

294
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:50,580
Since we're broken up now,

295
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:52,040
I'm giving it back to you.

296
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:54,120
Returning it to its rightful owner.

297
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:55,560
I don't want it.

298
00:15:55,560 --> 00:15:56,220
You keep it.

299
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:57,900
Then I'll smash it.

300
00:15:58,160 --> 00:15:59,040
Don't you dare.

301
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:01,040
If anyone smashes it, it should be me.

302
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:02,400
You don't even like it, so I'm smashing it.

303
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:03,760
I'll smash it! Give it to me!

304
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:04,760
I want to smash it.

305
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,240
Alright, you two, stop arguing.

306
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:06,800
I'm smashing it.

307
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:07,530
Give it to me.

308
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:09,120
I'm going to smash it!

309
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:10,640
Stop arguing!

310
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:11,560
Why? I want to smash it!

311
00:16:11,560 --> 00:16:12,280
Stop arguing.

312
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:13,720
Why should I? Listen to me.

313
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:14,450
Give it to me.

314
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:17,250
If you keep arguing, I'll smash it!

315
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,720
There's no point if you smash it.

316
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:20,560
Either I smash it,

317
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:21,680
or he does.

318
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,020
Look at you two.

319
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:25,640
How many times have I seen you break up?

320
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:26,960
You want to break up, right?

321
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:28,490
Then do it for good tonight.

322
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:30,020
Otherwise,

323
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:31,240
make up.

324
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:41,040
You...

325
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:43,020
How did you hurt your hand?

326
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,530
After you left that day,

327
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,960
I wanted to find the crystal ball and return it to you.

328
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:51,020
So we could just go our separate ways.

329
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:52,120
But,

330
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:57,560
when searching the cabinet, I accidentally knocked over a box.

331
00:16:57,560 --> 00:16:59,240
A utility knife fell out of it,

332
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:00,560
and cut me.

333
00:17:06,599 --> 00:17:08,460
When I packed up and left that day,

334
00:17:09,599 --> 00:17:11,329
I specifically took it with me.

335
00:17:12,359 --> 00:17:14,119
I was afraid you'd get emotional

336
00:17:14,119 --> 00:17:14,880
and smash it.

337
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:17,640
But aren't you going to smash it now anyway?

338
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:20,880
Because I just felt

339
00:17:24,359 --> 00:17:26,160
that you didn't want me anymore.

340
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:28,920
You're the one who didn't want me anymore!

341
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:31,320
How could I ever

342
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:34,000
bear to lose you?

343
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:35,220
Then...

344
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:36,480
let's make up.

345
00:17:37,320 --> 00:17:38,120
Why didn't you

346
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:41,280
say this earlier?

347
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:45,360
I'm sorry.

348
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:46,440
I was wrong.

349
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:47,600
Glad you guys made up.

350
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:49,720
You can't throw my things away anymore.

351
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:51,320
I know.

352
00:17:51,560 --> 00:17:53,960
But stop getting mad at me all the time.

353
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:55,840
I put the crystal ball back for you.

354
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:57,640
Do you get where I'm coming from?

355
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:58,600
I do.

356
00:17:58,600 --> 00:17:59,560
I was angry too.

357
00:17:59,560 --> 00:18:00,400
Do you get where I'm coming from?

358
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:01,320
Remember to take it.

359
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:01,680
I know.

360
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:02,640
Sorry.

361
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:03,040
But

362
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:05,320
I don't want to break up.

363
00:21:10,840 --> 00:21:11,640
Really great.

364
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:16,440
Cousin.

365
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:22,200
I can't push it, bro.

366
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:22,880
Wait a minute.

367
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:23,840
Push harder, bro.

368
00:21:23,840 --> 00:21:25,370
I'm going back to recharge.

369
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:27,680
What?

370
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:29,560
Look.

371
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:33,970
Bro, you watch here.

372
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:36,440
I'll go back and call the others.

373
00:21:37,120 --> 00:21:37,720
It's fine.

374
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:39,640
Leave it to me.

375
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:43,480
Hello.

376
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:46,360
I want to talk to you for a moment.

377
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:48,970
Thank you for liking me.

378
00:21:49,320 --> 00:21:50,560
This isn't

379
00:21:50,800 --> 00:21:52,400
the first time I've encountered this.

380
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:54,360
There are plenty of my photos online.

381
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:55,760
You don't have to do this.

382
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:59,080
I hope you can be a rational fan.

383
00:21:59,840 --> 00:22:01,040
I'd like to invite you

384
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:02,360
to join my fan club,

385
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:03,440
okay?

386
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:07,320
You can say whatever you want about me,

387
00:22:07,320 --> 00:22:08,600
but don't insult my taste.

388
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:08,920
Bro.

389
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:09,840
A trash singer like you,

390
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:11,920
what right do you have to insult our musical theater circle?

391
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:12,240
You!

392
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:14,680
Let go!

393
00:22:15,840 --> 00:22:16,560
My nose!

394
00:22:16,560 --> 00:22:17,160
Don't run!

395
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:18,240
Bro!

396
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:20,360
Where did you get hit?

397
00:22:20,720 --> 00:22:21,980
Is your nose okay, Shu?

398
00:22:24,720 --> 00:22:25,400
How are you?

399
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:27,440
I'm fine.

400
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,160
Are you hurt anywhere else?

401
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:29,760
No.

402
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:32,240
I've already installed cameras.

403
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:33,920
I didn't expect her to be so bold

404
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:35,840
as to attack in broad daylight.

405
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:38,200
How can there be a fan like this

406
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:39,400
who hits their own idol?

407
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:40,400
Exactly.

408
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:41,680
Director,

409
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:45,000
I think the situation is completely out of control now.

410
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:47,530
I suggest we clear out all the fans at the door.

411
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:49,840
This has never happened before.

412
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:51,800
I don't know what's wrong with them.

413
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:53,400
It's not your fault the fans are causing trouble.

414
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:54,920
It's your management team's fault.

415
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:56,560
It's their lack of strict management.

416
00:22:56,560 --> 00:22:57,960
Don't speak too soon.

417
00:22:58,640 --> 00:22:59,560
Am I wrong?

418
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:02,360
If the fans are causing trouble, isn't it your problem?

419
00:23:02,360 --> 00:23:03,840
If they are Jinxi's fans,

420
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:06,240
then of course it's our management team's fault.

421
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:07,700
But is there a possibility

422
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:10,800
that this whole thing has been fishy from the start?

423
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:13,400
We all thought Jinxi's poster was stolen

424
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:14,800
simply because his fans

425
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:16,000
wanted that picture.

426
00:23:16,640 --> 00:23:18,360
But is there another possibility?

427
00:23:18,360 --> 00:23:19,360
It's this person.

428
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:22,560
She just doesn't want Jin Xi to appear on this poster.

429
00:23:24,760 --> 00:23:25,960
What do you mean?

430
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:29,100
After the photo was cut out from Jin Xi's poster,

431
00:23:29,360 --> 00:23:31,640
only the posters of Bai Feixin

432
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:34,240
and Du Heying were left in the corridor.

433
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,440
That doesn't make sense.

434
00:23:35,440 --> 00:23:37,240
Why would a fan of Jin Xi

435
00:23:37,240 --> 00:23:38,400
hate Jin Xi?

436
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:41,080
Once all impossibilities are eliminated,

437
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:44,000
the truth will reveal itself.

438
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:48,840
I tore this off the fan

439
00:23:48,840 --> 00:23:49,970
who attacked Jin Xi.

440
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:52,530
Look at this.

441
00:24:01,800 --> 00:24:02,840
This is me playing

442
00:24:02,840 --> 00:24:05,240
Lu Mengzheng in 'Cailou Ji' five years ago.

443
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:08,000
So this isn't Jinxi's fan,

444
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:09,440
but yours, Du Heying.

445
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:12,040
Y-

446
00:24:12,080 --> 00:24:12,560
Yours.

447
00:24:14,840 --> 00:24:15,600
Mr. Heying.

448
00:24:17,640 --> 00:24:18,000
Y-

449
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:18,480
Yours.

450
00:24:23,160 --> 00:24:24,880
Didn't you say Jinxi should be held responsible

451
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:26,480
for her fans' actions?

452
00:24:26,720 --> 00:24:27,240
Then shouldn't you also be held responsible

453
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:29,400
for your fan's actions now?

454
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:31,760
She not only caused property damage to the theater troupe.

455
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:33,290
And you also hurt our Jinxi.

456
00:24:33,360 --> 00:24:35,720
Shouldn't you compensate for all of this?

457
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:38,160
This is not just Mr. Heying's fault.

458
00:24:38,800 --> 00:24:40,800
We all misunderstood Jinxi before.

459
00:24:40,840 --> 00:24:41,240
And...

460
00:24:41,240 --> 00:24:41,700
Xiaoqi.

461
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:44,320
Say no more.

462
00:24:51,840 --> 00:24:53,970
This incident was indeed caused by me.

463
00:24:58,840 --> 00:24:59,480
Everyone.

464
00:25:01,240 --> 00:25:02,640
Please give me some time.

465
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:05,690
I will give you all an explanation.

466
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:08,220
Mr. Heying.

467
00:25:08,560 --> 00:25:09,020
Heying.

468
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:09,900
Mr. Heying.

469
00:25:10,280 --> 00:25:10,960
Heying.

470
00:25:11,920 --> 00:25:12,400
Heying.

471
00:26:23,640 --> 00:26:24,240
Director.

472
00:26:24,720 --> 00:26:25,920
This is too unfair.

473
00:26:26,320 --> 00:26:28,250
Isn't this too much for Mr. Heying?

474
00:26:28,760 --> 00:26:31,000
Wasn't he going too far when he treated us like that before?

475
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:31,400
But this is...

476
00:26:31,400 --> 00:26:32,120
Calm down.

477
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:33,960
Let's wait until Heying comes back

478
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:35,360
and discuss it together.

479
00:26:36,280 --> 00:26:37,280
Speaking of which,

480
00:26:37,280 --> 00:26:38,560
Brother Heying has been out for a long time.

481
00:26:38,560 --> 00:26:39,760
Why isn't he back yet?

482
00:26:40,920 --> 00:26:41,920
Let's go find him.

483
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:46,720
Heying!

484
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:49,200
Mr. Heying!

485
00:26:49,200 --> 00:26:49,720
Heying!

486
00:26:50,880 --> 00:26:51,640
Mr. Heying!

487
00:26:54,160 --> 00:26:55,000
Mr. Heying!

488
00:26:55,360 --> 00:26:56,040
Where did he go?
